<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Echo (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>echo &lt;text&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>echo The ground trembles, and a deep voice rumbles from below.
</pre>
<p>Shows your text, just as you write it, to everyone in the room who is 
awake, yourself included. No name is added, so it reads like something 
happening in the world: a fine toy for a god running a quest or setting a 
scene.
</p><p>It is logged. To reach the whole game, use <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Broadcast</a>; to reach 
one person, <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Message</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Broadcast</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Message</a>
</pre>




</div>